# Restart dev servers in Replit

This workspace runs on Replit. App processes are managed workflows supervised by the platform. Restart them there.

Managed workflows:

- `artifacts/atg-consulting: web`
- `artifacts/api-server: API Server`
- `artifacts/mockup-sandbox: Component Preview Server`

When a server needs a restart, restart that Replit workflow. Leave its `PORT`, `BASE_PATH`, and proxy host as Replit set them.

Do not kill a managed process and start a replacement from the shell (`vite`, `pnpm dev`, `pnpm --filter … run dev`, or `node`). Do not bind a server to `127.0.0.1` or `localhost`, and do not verify the app at `http://127.0.0.1:<port>`.

Open and verify the app through the Replit preview URL or the shared proxy. Hostname-derived config, including the Clerk publishable key, follows the page host. A localhost host makes that config point at an address that does not exist.

One-off commands that are not the dev server — typecheck, tests, installs, builds — can still run in the shell.
